  "_note": "VulcanBench v4: 23 tasks whose upstream fixes ALL merged after 2026-05-31, making the suite contamination-clean for models with a May 2026 training cutoff (Claude Opus 5). Built because v3 decayed: 13 of its 23 tasks pre-date that cutoff. Ten v3 tasks already post-dated it and are carried forward unchanged (repo, tests and gold patch identical; only decontaminated/upstream_merged relabeled). Thirteen are new, sourced from PRs merged 2026-06-10 or later across ten upstream projects. Language mix matches v3: Python 9, Rust 4, TypeScript 4, JavaScript 3, Go 3. Grading discipline is unchanged from v3 (>=3 fail_to_pass verified failing at base, pass_to_pass guard that compiles and passes at base, behavior asserted via public APIs and never exact error text, acceptance constants generated from the gold patch). EVERY task records `upstream_merged`, so when a newer model's cutoff moves past these dates the clean subset is a query rather than an archaeology exercise -- do not assume this suite stays clean indefinitely. All 23 gated by scripts/validate_tasks.py --sandbox docker: gold=1.0, pre-patch=0.0, deterministic over 3 runs. Note oss-time-strftime-truncated-padding needs vulcanbench/sandbox:rust-2024 (rustc 1.90) rather than :rust (1.87), which is pinned for v3 reproducibility.",
